From 1bbe8563815248ca591c0a79efea1352cd7b22ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:26:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0043] thermal: core: optional time-separated confirmation of
 critical crossings (Hisense A9)

CONFIG_THERMAL_CRITICAL_CONFIRM_SAMPLES (default 1 = unchanged) makes the
thermal core require N consecutive samples at or above a zone's lowest
critical trip, each counted only if taken at least THERMAL_RECHECK_DELAY
(250 ms) after the previous counted one, before it crosses that trip.
Updates arriving sooner (sensor interrupt threads, sysfs reads, polling)
are discarded uncounted. While confirming, the driver's trip window is set
to (trip - 1, INT_MAX), so a level-triggered threshold interrupt is cleared
and cannot storm, and the zone is re-read when the next sample is due. A
sample below the trip, a failed read, an invalid-temperature sentinel, a
mode change and zone (re)initialisation (registration, resume) restart the
count. Genuine heat acts after (N - 1) * 250 ms plus scheduling delay.

KUnit (drivers/thermal/.kunitconfig): a scripted zone through
thermal_zone_device_update(): an interrupt storm of 50 identical high
samples counts once; sustained heat acts once within 500..1500 ms; the
sentinel, errno and mode-change resets. Reviews 24/28 (sensors).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
